1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:07,993
At Koware headquarters in New Legon, James Evans discovers four versions of an urgent notice from Kuala Lumpur.

2
00:00:10,450 --> 00:00:18,096
The building manager found a distribution register, but no original order, and no record showing who approved it.

3
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:27,984
Steven Sarpong separates the facts: delivery is documented. The authority behind the directions is not.

4
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:38,065
James sees a teaching opportunity—and a dangerous trap. The wrong lesson could turn uncertainty into an instruction.

5
00:00:40,450 --> 00:00:47,943
Matthew Ebenezer enters with a lively outreach proposal, eager to make the unusual notice an unforgettable example.

6
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:57,997
But a colourful diagram could make an unverified direction look official. James asks what the audience might believe.

7
00:01:00,450 --> 00:01:06,573
Matthew sees the risk. No route can be shown as safe merely because it appears on a notice.

8
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:16,950
He removes the arrows. The demonstration will teach evidence—not suggest an evacuation route.

9
00:01:20,450 --> 00:01:26,892
In the research laboratory, Obed Ali compares the latest Millennium Probe reading with the earlier records.

10
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:39,075
Its dates shift intentionally. The founder designed it to calculate from historical references, current dates, and changing values.

11
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:49,120
The founder also established Koware’s cloned Edubeam, initially operated solely by London’s Micro Computer Technology Institute.

12
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:59,134
Historical, present, and Probe time remain separate. A calculated date never establishes where a deployed team actually stands.

13
00:02:00,450 --> 00:02:07,393
Enka Yamoah enters with his worn notebook, studying the unsigned notice before turning to his own invention.

14
00:02:10,450 --> 00:02:19,403
The register confirms distribution. The Probe offers a precise calculation. Neither by itself authorises a safety decision.

15
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:28,191
James reshapes the lesson around three questions: what was observed, what was inferred, and what was authorised?

16
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:37,943
The team keeps each record separate, refuses to endorse a route, and leaves Kuala Lumpur’s observers in place.

17
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:49,219
Matthew holds his outreach draft for review. The notice stays unsigned. The Probe keeps calculating. The question remains.

18
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:59,851
A distribution register proves that four translated emergency notices were delivered, while a changing Millennium Probe readout provides a precisely calculated date.

19
00:02:59,851 --> 00:03:13,599
What is the essential difference between evidence that something was recorded and evidence that an action has been authorised, and how should a responsible team handle each before making a safety decision?
